# --- emulator pipeline ---------------------------------------------------
#
# The tools/ scripts ARE tracked: they are how the emulator is reproduced.
# What is excluded is everything they generate, all of which is derived and
# most of which is large.
#
# The chain is:
#   make_ep_design.py     -> ep_design.txt          (deterministic, regenerable)
#   ep_training.slurm     -> tools/ep_data/         (~60 MB of Monte Carlo)
#   train_ep_emulator.py  -> fit_*.npz              (intermediate)
#   emit_ep_weights.py    -> ep_emulator_weights.h  (TRACKED: the artifact)
#
# Only the last is committed. It records its own provenance in a header
# comment, and the scripts above regenerate every step from scratch.

tools/ep_data/
tools/ep_res_data/
tools/camb_spectra/
ep_design.txt
ep_resolution.txt
*.npz

# The second-attempt pipeline in research/ follows the same rule: the scripts
# are tracked, everything they generate is not.
#
#   research.ep.design      -> ep_design.jsonl      (deterministic, regenerable)
#   research/ep_campaign.slurm -> ep_data/          (the Monte Carlo)
#   research/fit.py         -> fit_*.npz            (intermediate)
ep_design.jsonl
ep_data/
logs/
